rm":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":"`dirichletSolution Ω lam mu f := if h : ∃ u, trace u = f ∧ WeakSolution u then Classical.choose h else f.out` and `DN f g := energy (dirichletSolution f) g.out` (Quot.out representatives of the trace classes); H¹ and traces hand-built as closures of smooth jets in L² and `Quot (SameTrace)`, strain and divergence from jets, energy = ∫ λ div u div v + 2μ ε(u):ε(v)","gap":null,"note":"`MainClaim`: for every open connected bounded smooth domain Ω ⊂ ℝ³ and two pairs of Lamé moduli smooth in a neighbourhood of the closure with μ > 0 and 3λ+2μ > 0 on the closure, equality of the full displacement-to-traction pairing `DN` as a function on all pairs of boundary data forces λ₁ = λ₂ and μ₁ = μ₂ on Ω; no analyticity, near-constant or near-boundary assumption. The `Classical.choose` in `dirichletSolution` picks the weak Dirichlet solution but only enters `DN` through energy against it, which is well defined because that solution is a weak solution (unique under the stated positivity); the fallback `f.out` is used only when no solution exists.","reading":"reading:baedf5c4548477eafe035954","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:653078eb033429529db8c63b","reading:baedf5c4548477eafe035954"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"6f7e5bf965eb85fac44ec93860c456b6a510b344","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c062