ε(v)","note":"`MainClaim`: for every open connected bounded smooth domain Ω ⊂ ℝ³ and two pairs of Lamé moduli smooth in a neighbourhood of the closure with μ > 0 and 3λ+2μ > 0 on the closure, equality of the full displacement-to-traction pairing `DN` as a function on all pairs of boundary data forces λ₁ = λ₂ and μ₁ = μ₂ on Ω; no analyticity, near-constant or near-boundary assumption. The `Classical.choose` in `dirichletSolution` picks the weak Dirichlet solution but only enters `DN` through energy against it, which is well defined because that solution is a weak solution (unique under the stated positivity); the fallback `f.out` is used only when no solution exists.","text":"The challenge statements imply the headline claim after unpacking definitions or one routine step.","url":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet/blob/14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db/reviews/openai-math/fidelity-table.csv","verdict":"full"},"source_verdict":"full","state":"all","target":"f:372","target_kind":"family-headline"}],"release_id":"openai-math","remaining_checks":[{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:fcac2bf72903ead614e5f9884b632a88f81737cee33995f595fb442750c48f51","grain":"challenge","id":"challenge:ElasticityUniqueness","title":"ElasticityUniqueness"},"kind":"scope-review","reason":"An AI scope draft has no named human review.","target":"l:ElasticityUniqueness"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:6ea9f3a4d0e1b6b163a01c3c2d61c72fa22211f7a664c7c37d78100e37a7b30d","grain":"family","id":"family:372","title":"Global uniqueness in smooth isotropic elasticity"},"kind":"claim-identification","reason":"Lexical navigation candidate; catalogue headline identity requires review.","target":"f:372"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:6ea9f3a4d0e1b6b163a01c3c2d61c72fa22211f7a664c7c37d78100e37a7b30d","grain":"family","id":"family:372","title":"Global uniqueness in smooth isotropic elasticity"},"credit":{"atlas_pin":"6f7e5bf965eb85fac44ec93860c456b6a510b344","autho